@startuml
title POST /api/v1/games/{game_id}/result
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "SQLAlchemy session" as DB
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: POST result {player_winner: ID or null}
API -> API: Validate required nullable winner and positive IDs
API -> DB: get_db(): request transaction
DB -> PG: Lock game FOR UPDATE
break Game missing
  DB -> PG: ROLLBACK
  API --> Client: 404
end
DB -> PG: Select existing result
break Existing result has a different winner
  DB -> PG: ROLLBACK
  API --> Client: 409
end
alt Identical result already exists
  PG --> DB: Original result (reuse ID)
  DB --> API: Original result; status 200
else No result exists
  opt Non-null winner
    DB -> PG: Find player with this ID and game_id
    break Winner absent or belongs to another game
      DB -> PG: ROLLBACK
      API --> Client: 422
    end
  end
  note over DB: Explicit null winner records a draw
  DB -> PG: Insert game_result; flush
  PG --> DB: New result with generated ID
  DB --> API: New result; status 201
end
API -> API: Validate / serialize GameResult
API -> DB: Exit request transaction
DB -> PG: COMMIT
API --> Client: 200 original result / 201 new result
note over API, PG
Game lock serializes completion and player replacement.
Other validation and database failures: see transaction.puml.
end note
@enduml
